{
  "about": "Curated mapping from free-exercise-db (Unlicense) to the Workout OS exercise library. Read by scripts/build-exercises.mjs. Keys are our exercise ids. source_id null means a custom entry (no good upstream match). Omitted fields fall back to the rules in the build script: increment_kg by equipment, step_kg = increment_kg (5 for lower body barbell and trap bar lifts), per_hand for dumbbell and kettlebell, bodyweight for bodyweight equipment, measure reps, instructions cleaned from the source.",
  "tag_glossary": {
    "knee_friendly": "Knee dominant movement with supported, controllable depth (hack squat, leg press, step-up, reverse lunge). Only knee dominant exercises carry it, so the knee_friendly limitation never swaps a hinge for a squat.",
    "deep_knee_flexion": "Free barbell squat that takes the knee into deep flexion under heavy load (back squat, front squat). Goblet and split squats stay neutral: light load, self-selected depth.",
    "low_spinal_load": "Little axial or shear load on the spine: supported, seated, lying, machine or light upright work.",
    "high_spinal_load": "Heavy axial or shear load on the spine: barbell squats, deadlifts, RDLs, good mornings, bent-over rows.",
    "unilateral": "Each side's working muscles move their own load, so the stronger side cannot take over: single-limb work, and dumbbell, kettlebell or single-handle presses, rows and carries. Isolation and core exercises are not tagged, so the shoulder_symmetry limitation swaps the big pressing and rowing lifts and leaves accessories alone.",
    "shoulder_friendly": "Pressing or pulling path that is usually easy on the shoulder (landmine press, neutral grip pulldown, face pull, rear delt work).",
    "overhead": "Arms extended overhead under load (overhead presses, overhead triceps extensions). Pull-ups and pulldowns are not tagged.",
    "machine": "Machine equipment (added automatically for equipment machine).",
    "bodyweight": "Bodyweight exercise where logged weight is added load (added automatically when bodyweight is true).",
    "assisted": "Logged weight is assistance: more weight makes it easier. Progress by reps, not load.",
    "grip": "Grip is often the limiting factor (carries, deadlifts, hanging work)."
  },
